From df849eee240d8b861321170b32b04575b1ac63f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 02:52:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04778/11362] [outer-loop] Quarantine hanging tests 4940/4941
 that stalled the .457 milestone transition
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Watchdog 2026-06-29: the milestone .456->.457 archive/activate TRANSITION task (experiment_4957)
FAILED twice (04:04, 05:27 UTC) with "Codex CLI error: Hard wall-clock cap after 4801s" — a conductor
stall loop. Root cause: experiment_4957's pretest gate is `pytest tests/python -q` (the FULL suite), and
two new .457 tests HANG it:
  - test_experiment_4940_distributional_energy_verifier_executable_spec.py
  - test_experiment_4941_bank_and_pivot_audit.py
Each runs 30 tests then hangs on the last item: a test invokes mod.main(...) which executes the REAL
distributional-energy dry-run (model/FoVer-ensemble/data I/O) instead of mocking it. The full-suite gate
therefore never returns -> codex polls it for 70+min -> wall-clock cap -> FAIL -> retry -> repeat (a
70-min CPU-bound pytest-xdist run + zombies was hammering 4 cores; killed it to free CPU + diagnose).

Fix: quarantine both files via conftest collect_ignore (the documented last-resort mechanism for tests
that stall the conductor pre-test gate; same pattern as the existing 1029/1031/1043 + semantic_energy_probe
entries). Verified: `pytest tests/python --collect-only` now completes (113s, 43704 tests, no hang) and the
two files are excluded. Proper follow-up: mock the model/data I/O in mod.main for these two tests (their
network-checker tests are already correctly monkeypatched).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
